    {
      "name" : "updated_coll_of_coll_compatible_reference_item-accept#10",
      "script" : "[U11] `Coll[Coll[Int]](Coll(1)).updated(0, Coll[Long](1L))` — a REFERENCE-backed array (`[Lsigma.Coll;`), so the store only checks the item's CLASS, and a `Coll` is a `Coll`: it **RETURNS** at cost 100, and the result holds an item of the wrong item type. The complement of U1-U10: an ill-typed item is rejected by a primitive array and WAVED THROUGH by an Object array. An implementation that type-checks items uniformly over-rejects here.",
